<title>PAKISTAN: HOCKEY-GOLDEN JUBILEE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-GOLDEN JUBILEE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result on the fifth day of the</p>
<p>Golden Jubilee of Pakistan men's hockey tournament on Thursday:</p>
<p>Australia beat England 5-2 (halftime 3-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Matthew Smith 24, Jay Stacy 31, 34,62, James</p>
<p>Elmer</p>
<p>70</p>
<p>England - Russell Garcia 5, Bob Crutchley 13</p>
<p>Played earlier:</p>
<p>Germany 3 Pakistan 3 (halftime 1-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Germany - Bjorn Michel 30, Oliver Domke 41, Kai</p>
<p>Hollensteiner 49</p>
<p>Pakistan- Tahir Zaman 19 penalty stroke, Muhammad Shahbaz</p>
<p>24,</p>
<p>Kamran Ashraf 69</p>
<p>    Standings  P   W   D   L   F     A   PTS</p>
<p>Netherlands    3   2   1   0   12    5   7</p>
<p>Germany	  3   2   1   0    7    4   7</p>
<p>Pakistan	 3   0   3   0    7    7   3</p>
<p>Australia	3   1   0   2    8    7   2</p>
<p>England	  4   0   1   3    3   14   1</p>
<p>Netherlands and Germany qualify for Sunday's final</p>
</text>
